Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] Items screen: no icon for the item panel before an item is chosen

Owner report (OLED, EU, preview.30-rc6): the game crashed on opening the
Items screen after several battles. Root cause, reproduced on the PC host
(US and EU, any Text speed, and on v0.6.5-preview.29 too): any non-empty item
list crashes the field menu's first screen with a SIGSEGV in getItemCategory.
The Switch crash_report.txt agrees: mode_file 0x207 (EU STSTATUS), data abort
at far=0xd (ItemInfo.type of a NULL ItemInfo), x0=0, pc == lr and
x1 == pc - 0xc, which is the shape of getItemCategory (`bl getItem` returns
NULL, the next instruction is `ldrb w1, [x0, #13]`). The pc does not
symbolize cleanly against the ELF we kept (addr2line names a neighbouring
function), so the rest of this note rests on the host reproduction.

STSTATUS_runItemScreen substate 12 (STSTATUS_openItemList) creates the item
list task and, in the same frame, starts the item panel's fade
(STSTATUS_fadeItemInfo(screen, 1), 10 frames). STSTATUS_drawItemScreen draws
the panel's icon, sprite ITEM_FUNCS.getCategory(screen->item), as soon as
that fade is full, which is 11 updates later. The list task sets
screen->item (STSTATUS_refreshItemList) only when its own two fades are
done: one frame to fill the list, one to start them, 11 updates, so two
frames after the panel is full. For those two frames screen->item is 0
(createTask zeroes the screen), getItem(0) is NULL and getItemCategory reads
the item's type through it. The PS1 reads kernel RAM there and draws some
icon for two frames; a 64-bit host faults. An empty list never gets here
(the screen shows "No Items." and does not open the panel), which is why
the new-game bag and the replay scenarios never hit it.

Under PORT_HOST the icon is skipped while screen->item is not a valid item
(<= 0). The panel frame is drawn as before and the icon appears the frame
the list chooses its first item, as on the PS1 minus two frames of an
arbitrary icon. Nothing else changes: with an item chosen (every frame
after, and every reopen of the list, where screen->item is kept) the same
sprite is drawn. The null-guard diagnostic (port_null_guard.h) reports the
site as "item_screen.icon-no-item" in PC Debug and nxlink builds.

diff -ruN a/src/menus/field_menu/item_screen.c b/src/menus/field_menu/item_screen.c
--- a/src/menus/field_menu/item_screen.c
+++ b/src/menus/field_menu/item_screen.c
@@ -2,6 +2,10 @@
    (STSTATUS_createItemScreen): its rodata starts at 0x800829D0 (USA). */
 
 #include "menus/field_menu.h"
+#if PORT_HOST
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include "port_null_guard.h"
+#endif
 
 /* Creates the first screen's windows */
 void STSTATUS_createItemWindows(ItemScreen *screen, ItemScreenWindows *windows) {
@@ -377,7 +381,21 @@
         } else {
             sprite.setScale(ONE, ONE, ONE);
             sprite.setTexture(0x140, 0);
+#if PORT_HOST
+            /* The panel's fade (10 frames) is started together with the list's task,
+               which only sets `screen->item` when its own fades are done, two or three
+               frames later. In between the item is 0 and getItem(0) is NULL: the PS1
+               reads the item's type through NULL (kernel RAM) and draws some icon for
+               two frames, a 64-bit host faults. Draw no icon until an item is chosen. */
+            if (screen->item <= 0) {
+                DW3_NULL_GUARD_HIT("item_screen.icon-no-item");
+                fprintf(stderr, "dw3: items screen: panel icon skipped, no item chosen yet (patch 0069)\n");
+            } else {
+#endif
             sprite.draw(FILE_CACHE.getEntry(FILE_MENU_SPRITES << 16), ITEM_FUNCS.getCategory(screen->item), 0x16, 0xAE);
+#if PORT_HOST
+            }
+#endif
         }
         sprite.setTexture(0x280, 0x100);
         sprite.draw(FILE_CACHE.getEntry(FILE_STATUS_SPRITES << 16), 0x2F, 0xF, 0xA5);
